<title>ITALY: Italy January producer prices rose 0.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Italy January producer prices rose 0.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics office ISTAT gave the following Italian producer price data for January.</p>
<p>    PRODUCER PRICES	   Jan 97    Dec 96	 Jan 96</p>
<p>    Year/year change	 +0.9 pct   +0.9 pct(r)  +5.9 pct</p>
<p>    Month/month change     +0.3 pct    0.0 pct(r)  +0.3 pct</p>
<p>    Index (base 1995=100)    102.6     102.3	  101.7</p>
<p>Note: ISTAT said it had changed the base of the index to 1995 from 1990 previously.  </p>
<p>Istat gave the following general breakdown:</p>
<p>				  Mo/Mo change (%)    Yr/Yr change (%)</p>
<p>    Consumer goods		  +0.1		   +1.0</p>
<p>    Investment goods		+0.1		   +2.3</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods	    +0.5		   +0.6</p>
<p>It gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown:</p>
<p>    Sector			    mo/mo (%)	     yr/yr (%)</p>
<p>    Energy products		 +1.3		    +6.4</p>
<p>    Minerals and metals	   +0.1		    +2.8</p>
<p>    Non-metal minerals	    +0.6		    +2.3</p>
<p>    Chemicals			 +1.2		    +0.9</p>
<p>    Metal works		     +0.2		    +2.8</p>
<p>    Cars and parts		  -0.7		    +2.3</p>
<p>    Food, drink and tobacco     -0.3		    -1.0</p>
<p>    Clothing, leather goods     -0.1		    -0.2</p>
<p>    Other goods		     +0.2		    +2.6</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
